<title>USA: TABLE-Handy &amp; Harman Q2 net income rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Handy &amp; Harman Q2 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 Months</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			   $0.59		    $0.32</p>
<p> Net			  $7,009		   $4,454</p>
<p> Revs		     $115,971		 $105,806</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   11,957		   14,023</p>
<p>	  6 Months</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.93     loss	 $0.06</p>
<p> Net			$11,096     loss	  $837</p>
<p> Revs		    $220,903		 $214,146</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  11,973		   14,027</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: -- As a result of reductions in the quantities of precious metal inventories valued under the LIFO method of accounting, Q2 1997 results include an after-tax gain of $2.7 million or $0.23 per share.</p>
<p>-- Company says excluding LIFO gain, profit contribution increased 13 percent over Q@ 1996.  Increase primarily attributable to the results of Olympic Manufacturing Group Inc acquired on Feb 28, 1997 and partially offset by a decrease in contribution from the Specialty Tubing Group caused by continued weakness in the semiconductor fabrication industry.</p>
</text>
